#
# Counter-example: a math:SimplicialComplex whose codimension-2 diamond IS
# combinatorially complete (coface cX has two distinct codimension-1 faces bY, bW,
# each a codimension-1 face of far-face aZ), so the combinatorial simplicial check
# math:BoundarySquareZeroConstraint is SATISFIED (a distinct partner face exists on
# both traversals). But the reified ±1 math:CellIncidence records carry the WRONG
# (non-induced) orientation: both composition sign products are +1, so the finite
# signed sum Σ_b [cX:b]·[b:aZ] = (+1)·(+1) + (+1)·(+1) = +2 ≠ 0 — ∂∘∂ ≠ 0. It fires
# math:GeneralBoundarySquareZeroConstraint (the logic:JoinAggregateConstraint,
# shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent → math:BrokenBoundarySquareZero) and NO other
# finding. This isolates the composition point of the two enforcement layers: the
# combinatorial diamond check does not read signs (and passes here), while the general
# signed-sum check catches the orientation error — so a signed simplicial complex is
# covered by math:GeneralBoundarySquareZeroConstraint (onClass math:Cell), never left
# unchecked by the unsigned diamond constraint. Every cell declares its
# math:cellDimension and it is not a math:CochainComplex.

@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/simplicial-signed-noncancelling/> .

ex:broken a math:SimplicialComplex ;
    math:hasCell ex:cX , ex:bY , ex:bW , ex:aZ .

ex:dim0 a math:NaturalNumber ; math:inNumberSystem math:naturalNumbers ; math:isExact true .
ex:dim1 a math:NaturalNumber ; math:inNumberSystem math:naturalNumbers ; math:isExact true .
ex:dim2 a math:NaturalNumber ; math:inNumberSystem math:naturalNumbers ; math:isExact true .

# The complete diamond over the unsigned face relation: cX ▷ {bY, bW} ▷ aZ, so
# math:BoundarySquareZeroConstraint's ∃-partner check is satisfied on both paths.
ex:cX a math:Cell ; math:cellDimension ex:dim2 ; math:incidentTo ex:bY , ex:bW .
ex:bY a math:Cell ; math:cellDimension ex:dim1 ; math:incidentTo ex:aZ .
ex:bW a math:Cell ; math:cellDimension ex:dim1 ; math:incidentTo ex:aZ .
ex:aZ a math:Cell ; math:cellDimension ex:dim0 .

# The signed incidence records the general SUM constraint scores. The induced
# orientation would pair opposite signs; here BOTH products are +1, so the group
# (cX, aZ) sums to +2 ≠ 0.
ex:incCXbY a math:CellIncidence ; math:incidenceCoface ex:cX ; math:incidenceFace ex:bY ; math:incidenceSign 1 .
ex:incCXbW a math:CellIncidence ; math:incidenceCoface ex:cX ; math:incidenceFace ex:bW ; math:incidenceSign 1 .
ex:incbYaZ a math:CellIncidence ; math:incidenceCoface ex:bY ; math:incidenceFace ex:aZ ; math:incidenceSign 1 .
ex:incbWaZ a math:CellIncidence ; math:incidenceCoface ex:bW ; math:incidenceFace ex:aZ ; math:incidenceSign 1 .
